---
/*
 * Hallmark · system-managed (defers to .claude/CLAUDE.md "Digital Curator")
 * page: Mississauga wedding photographer (city landing) · money page for "wedding photographer mississauga"
 * S20 swap test: every venue fact, light window, permit line and price below traces to
 *   src/content/blog/glenerin-inn-wedding-photographer-guide.md,
 *   src/content/blog/adamson-estate-wedding-photography-guide.md,
 *   src/data/locations.json (adamson-estate), src/data/portfolio.json, src/data/packages.json,
 *   src/data/faq.json, or src/pages/services/wedding.astro. Nothing is generic to "a city".
 * S10 experience gate: only Glenerin Inn and Adamson Estate are claimed as Mississauga venues.
 *   Humber Bay is named as Etobicoke, which is what it is. Port Credit and Jack Darling were
 *   removed because no shoot or scout of either exists in the site data.
 * honest-copy: hero quote is the REAL Natalie + Shavar pullQuote from portfolio.json
 * no fabricated metrics/testimonials · no em/en dashes · tokens + components reused
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/seo/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../components/ui/FAQAccordion.astro';
import PortfolioFinalCTA from '../components/global/PortfolioFinalCTA.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import site from '../data/site.json';

import heroImage from '../assets/images/portfolio/natalie-shavar/03.jpg';
import whyImage from '../assets/images/portfolio/ayushi-parth-adamson/05.jpg';
import preWeddingImage from '../assets/images/portfolio/ayushi-parth-adamson/12.jpg';

// Two venues, because two is how many I have actually worked in this city.
// Every sentence here is lifted from the venue guide or the location guide, never invented.
const mississaugaVenues = [
  {
    name: 'The Glenerin Inn and Spa',
    href: '/blog/glenerin-inn-wedding-photographer-guide/',
    note: 'A stone estate inn sunk into a wooded ravine at 1695 The Collegeway, in Erindale near the UTM campus, about 30 minutes from downtown Toronto. The ceremony deck sits under a canopy of old growth maples, so mid to late afternoon light drops through the leaves in soft dappled patches, and no light I could rig comes close. Once the candles are lit the domed reception room takes over, arched windows and warm sconces, a second look without leaving the property. Photo access comes with your venue booking, so there is no public permit to chase. Write your photo window into the event order if you want early getting ready coverage or night portraits.',
    links: [{ href: '/portfolio/natalie-shavar/', label: 'A wedding I shot here' }],
  },
  {
    name: 'Adamson Estate',
    href: '/location-guide/adamson-estate/',
    note: 'A 1919 Colonial Revival stone manor at 850 Enola Avenue in Lakeview, sitting right on the Lake Ontario shoreline behind a low stone wall. I work it as a loop. The lakefront terrace first, because the bounce light off the water is strongest in the last two hours before sunset and fills faces with almost no hard shadow. Then the brick courtyards behind the house, where patterned walls and one deep archway give me three backdrops inside twenty feet. The City of Mississauga asks for a commercial photography permit for professional shoots, so call 905-615-4100 before you lock the date. Parking is a free lot on site, small, so arrive about twenty minutes early on a weekend.',
    links: [
      { href: '/blog/adamson-estate-wedding-photography-guide/', label: "Adamson photographer's guide" },
      { href: '/portfolio/ayushi-parth-adamson/', label: 'A session I shot here' },
    ],
  },
];

// Fast facts. Prices and hours from packages.json, travel and delivery from faq.json,
// delivery window cross-checked against services/wedding.astro, solo framing from Positioning.
const mississaugaFastFacts = [
  { label: 'Starting price', value: 'From $1,401.25 for The Essentials. Up to 6 hours on the day, unlimited edited photos, and an engagement session included.' },
  { label: 'Coverage lengths', value: '6, 10, or 14 hours depending on the collection, up to $3,801.25 for The Complete Story. The included engagement session runs 2 hours.' },
  { label: 'Travel to Mississauga', value: 'Included. Mississauga sits inside my GTA coverage, so there is no travel fee. Past the GTA I quote travel at cost, upfront.' },
  { label: 'Delivery', value: 'A sneak peek within days. The full gallery in 2 to 3 months. Priority 2 to 3 week delivery is available for an added fee.' },
  { label: 'How I work', value: 'Solo. One photographer, one wedding a day, prompting rather than posing, so the room stays yours.' },
];

const mississaugaFaq = [
  {
    question: 'Do you travel to Mississauga for weddings?',
    answer: 'Yes. Mississauga sits inside my GTA coverage, so travel to the city is included in every wedding collection and there is no separate fee. Past the GTA, travel is quoted at cost and agreed before you book.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Where do you take couple portraits in Mississauga?',
    answer: 'It depends on your venue. At The Glenerin Inn I stay on the property and move from the maple canopy over the ceremony deck to the stone facade and the ravine paths. At Adamson Estate I run a loop, the lakefront terrace first for the bounced light off the water, then the brick courtyards, then the back lawn for the wide frame at last light. If you want the Toronto skyline behind you, the Humber Bay Arch Bridge sits just east of the Mississauga line in Etobicoke, about twenty minutes from Lakeview.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do we need a permit to photograph at Adamson Estate?',
    answer: 'Yes. Adamson Estate is City of Mississauga property and the City asks for a commercial photography permit whenever a professional is hired. Personal phone photos are fine without one. Call the City at 905-615-4100 to confirm the current fee, and do it before you lock the date. The Glenerin Inn works the other way. It is private property, so your photo access comes with your venue booking and there is no public permit.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How far ahead should we book a Mississauga wedding photographer?',
    answer: 'As soon as the date and the venue are settled. I shoot solo and take one wedding a day, so a Saturday is either open or it is gone, and there is no waiting list behind it. Send me the date and I will tell you within 24 hours whether I still have it.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What happens if it rains on our Mississauga wedding day?',
    answer: 'I still shoot. The Glenerin Inn has a genuinely good rain plan, because the domed reception room with its arched windows and sconces carries an indoor ceremony without looking like a backup. Adamson Estate is the opposite, open lakefront with wind coming off the water, so there I move the portraits earlier in the day or shelter under the courtyard archway. Some of my favourite frames from that estate came from a gust catching a veil.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How much is a wedding photographer in Mississauga?',
    answer: 'Collections start at $1,401.25 for The Essentials, which is up to 6 hours with an engagement session included, and run to $3,801.25 for The Complete Story at up to 14 hours. Mississauga costs the same as a Toronto wedding because GTA travel is already in the price. The full breakdown sits on the wedding photography page.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you photograph small ceremonies and elopements in Mississauga?',
    answer: "Yes. Intimate coverage is the core of what I do. One photographer, shorter hours, smaller rooms, and no second shooter to work around. If you are planning a civil ceremony at a city clerk's office rather than a venue, that runs on its own shorter coverage and has its own page and pricing.",
  },
];

const businessRef = { '@id': `${site.url}/#business` };

const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Mississauga Wedding Photography',
  description: 'Wedding photography in Mississauga by AD Photography. Coverage at The Glenerin Inn in Erindale and Adamson Estate in Lakeview, solo, with GTA travel included.',
  provider: businessRef,
  areaServed: {
    '@type': 'City',
    name: 'Mississauga',
    address: { '@type': 'PostalAddress', addressRegion: 'ON', addressCountry: 'CA' },
  },
  serviceType: 'Wedding Photography',
  image: `${site.url}/og-default.jpg`,
  url: `${site.url}/wedding-photographer-mississauga/`,
};

const faqPageSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: mississaugaFaq.map((q) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: q.answer },
  })),
};

const jsonLd = [serviceSchema, faqPageSchema];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Wedding Photographer Mississauga: Glenerin Inn, Adamson"
  description="Wedding photographer in Mississauga covering the Glenerin Inn, Adamson Estate, and the Lakeshore waterfront. Real weddings, coverage from $1,401.25."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="sr-only">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Mississauga Wedding Photographer', href: '/wedding-photographer-mississauga/' },
    ]} />
  </div>

  <!-- ═══ HERO: real Mississauga couple quote + portrait ═══ -->
  <section style="padding-top: var(--spacing-block); padding-bottom: var(--spacing-block);">
    <div class="container-editorial">
      <div class="grid-editorial items-center" style="min-height: 80svh;">
        <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-5 reveal order-2 md:order-1">
          <p class="text-label-md text-on-surface-muted mb-6 eyebrow-rule">Mississauga · Wedding Photography</p>
          <blockquote class="text-display-md" style="max-width: 22ch;">
            "I keep going back to the one where I'm walking and my veil is flying everywhere. I didn't even know you took that."
          </blockquote>
          <p class="text-label-md text-on-surface-variant mt-8">Natalie &amp; Shavar</p>
          <p class="text-label-sm text-on-surface-muted">The Glenerin Inn and Spa, Mississauga</p>
          <div class="mt-8 flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
            <Button href="#investment" variant="primary">See Investment</Button>
            <Button href="/contact/?location=mississauga" variant="secondary">Start the Conversation</Button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="col-span-12 md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7 reveal-right stagger-2 order-1 md:order-2 mb-[var(--spacing-element)] md:mb-0">
          <div class="aspect-[3/4] overflow-hidden hover-zoom">
            <Image
              src={heroImage}
              alt="Natalie and Shavar hold hands beside her white ceremony bouquet at The Glenerin Inn in Mississauga, by AD Photography"
              widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
              sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw"
              quality={75}
              format="avif"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover parallax-img"
              loading="eager"
              fetchpriority="high"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="gallery-plaque">
            <div class="gallery-plaque__line">
              <span class="gallery-plaque__plate">Wedding</span>
              <span class="gallery-plaque__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="gallery-plaque__meta">The Glenerin Inn, Mississauga</span>
            </div>
            <p class="gallery-plaque__title">Natalie <em>&amp;</em> Shavar</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ WHY MISSISSAUGA (carries the H1) ═══ -->
  <section class="section-frame bg-surface-dim" style="padding: var(--spacing-section) 0;">
    <div class="container-editorial">
      <div class="grid-editorial items-center">
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-5 aspect-[3/4] overflow-hidden reveal-left hover-zoom order-2 lg:order-1 mt-10 lg:mt-0">
          <Image
            src={whyImage}
            alt="Ayushi and Parth touch fingertips against an open sky during their pre-wedding shoot at Adamson Estate, Mississauga, by AD Photography"
            widths={[400, 600, 800]}
            sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 42vw"
            class="w-full h-full object-cover parallax-img"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7 reveal stagger-2 order-1 lg:order-2">
          <p class="text-label-md text-on-surface-muted mb-6 eyebrow-rule">Why Mississauga</p>
          <h1 class="section-title char-reveal">Wedding photographer in <em>Mississauga.</em></h1>
          <p class="section-deck text-on-surface-variant mt-8 measure-wide">
            I work as a wedding photographer in Mississauga because of two properties at opposite ends of the city, and they ask opposite things of me. The Glenerin Inn is a stone estate down in a wooded ravine off The Collegeway in Erindale, roughly 30 minutes from downtown Toronto, and it holds an entire wedding under one roof. Adamson Estate is a 1919 stone manor on the Lake Ontario shoreline in Lakeview, and it trades the roof for water, ivy, and old brick.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-on-surface-variant mt-5 measure-wide">
            That is why I plan a Mississauga day backwards from sunset. At Adamson the last two hours before the sun drops are the whole session, because light bounces off the lake onto the stone and fills faces with almost no hard shadow. At Glenerin the window is mid to late afternoon, while the sun is still high enough to fall through the maple canopy over the ceremony deck. Same city, two completely different timelines.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-on-surface-variant mt-5 measure-wide">
            My name is <a href="/about/" class="underline-link">Akash Desai</a> and I am the only person you will meet on the day. I shoot solo and I prompt rather than pose, so nobody spends their afternoon being arranged. Most of what I book out here is the same shape as an <a href="/intimate-wedding-toronto/" class="underline-link">intimate Toronto wedding</a>, just with a ravine or a lakefront instead of a downtown block. Mississauga is inside my GTA coverage, so travel to the city is included and the day is priced exactly as a Toronto wedding would be.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ MISSISSAUGA VENUES ═══ -->
  <section class="section-frame bg-background" style="padding: var(--spacing-section) 0;">
    <div class="container-editorial">
      <div class="grid-editorial items-end" style="margin-bottom: var(--spacing-block);">
        <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-7">
          <p class="text-label-md text-on-surface-muted reveal eyebrow-rule mb-6">The Venues</p>
          <h2 class="section-title reveal stagger-1">Where I shoot in <em>Mississauga.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-5 md:col-start-8 mt-6 md:mt-0">
          <p class="section-deck text-on-surface-variant reveal stagger-2 measure-wide">
            Two properties, both of which I have worked from the inside. I would rather tell you the permit line and the good hour at two venues than list twelve I have only driven past.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ul class="venue-list reveal stagger-2">
        {mississaugaVenues.map((v) => (
          <li class="venue-row">
            <a href={v.href} class="venue-row__name text-heading-md font-serif cubic-ease" style="transition-duration: var(--duration-hover);">
              {v.name}
            </a>
            <p class="venue-row__note text-body-md text-on-surface-variant measure-wide">{v.note}</p>
            <p class="venue-row__links text-label-sm">
              {v.links.map((l, i) => (
                <>
                  {i > 0 && <span class="venue-row__sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>}
                  <a href={l.href} class="underline-link">{l.label}</a>
                </>
              ))}
            </p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ REAL MISSISSAUGA WEDDING (proof) ═══ -->
  <section class="section-frame bg-surface-dim" style="padding: var(--spacing-section) 0;">
    <div class="container-editorial">
      <div class="reveal" style="max-width: 60ch;">
        <p class="text-label-md text-on-surface-muted mb-6 eyebrow-rule">A Real Mississauga Wedding</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Natalie and Shavar at <em>Glenerin.</em></h2>
        <p class="section-deck text-on-surface-variant mt-8">
          They married on the ceremony deck on a September afternoon in 2025, white florals climbing a gold arch, the maples doing what they do to the light. Shavar was up there early with his groomsmen and his son, adjusting his bow tie, counting seconds. When Natalie came down the aisle on her father's arm the whole deck went quiet, and not the polite kind.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body-md text-on-surface-variant mt-5 measure-wide">
          Afterwards I walked them through the stone pathways for portraits and the wind kept lifting her veil. The frame she still talks about is a motion blur from that walk, which is the quote at the top of this page. By evening the whole party had moved inside under the dome with the candles lit and Shavar's grandmother on the microphone. One property, a garden ceremony and a candlelit reception, nobody in a car between them. That is the whole argument for Glenerin.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
          <Button href="/portfolio/natalie-shavar/" variant="primary">See their gallery</Button>
          <Button href="/blog/glenerin-inn-wedding-photographer-guide/" variant="secondary">Read the Glenerin guide</Button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-editorial items-center mt-12">
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-7 aspect-[16/10] overflow-hidden reveal hover-zoom">
          <Image
            src={preWeddingImage}
            alt="Ayushi cradles Parth's face for a kiss at the water's edge at Adamson Estate in Mississauga, by AD Photography"
            widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
            sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 58vw"
            class="w-full h-full object-cover parallax-img"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-4 lg:col-start-9 reveal stagger-2 mt-8 lg:mt-0">
          <p class="text-quote italic text-on-surface-variant">The other side of the city.</p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-on-surface-variant mt-4 measure-wide">
            Ayushi and Parth spent a clear spring afternoon on the Adamson grounds. Shoreline first, then the manor steps, then black tie in front of the green door as the light went amber. Their full afternoon is in the <a href="/portfolio/ayushi-parth-adamson/" class="underline-link">Adamson Estate gallery</a>, and the <a href="/blog/adamson-estate-wedding-photography-guide/" class="underline-link">Adamson photography guide</a> carries the permit line, the parking, and the five spots I return to.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ INVESTMENT + FAST FACTS (condensed, funnels to canonical service page) ═══ -->
  <section id="investment" class="section-frame bg-background" style="padding: var(--spacing-section) 0;">
    <div class="container-editorial">
      <div class="grid-editorial items-center">
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6 reveal">
          <p class="text-label-md text-on-surface-muted mb-6 eyebrow-rule">Investment</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">What a wedding photographer in <em>Mississauga</em> costs.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-5 lg:col-start-8 reveal stagger-2 mt-6 lg:mt-0">
          <p class="section-deck text-on-surface-variant measure-wide">
            The Essentials is $1,401.25 and covers up to 6 hours with the engagement session included. The Complete Story is $3,801.25 for up to 14 hours. Nothing about Mississauga changes those numbers, because GTA travel is already inside them.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-on-surface-variant mt-5 measure-wide">
            If the budget is the part you are still working out, I put the real arithmetic in my post on <a href="/blog/intimate-toronto-wedding-photography-cost/" class="underline-link">what an intimate wedding actually costs</a>. If your day is a signing at a city clerk's office rather than a venue, look at <a href="/services/civil-ceremony/" class="underline-link">civil ceremony coverage</a> instead, which runs shorter and is priced on its own.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-8">
            <Button href="/services/wedding/" variant="primary">See the full packages</Button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Fast facts: plain answers for search results and AI summaries. Every value is
           already stated in packages.json, faq.json, or the wedding service page. -->
      <div class="grid-editorial" style="margin-top: var(--spacing-block);">
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-10 lg:col-start-2 reveal stagger-3">
          <h2 class="text-label-sm text-on-surface-muted uppercase tracking-widest mb-6">Mississauga weddings at a glance</h2>
          <dl>
            {mississaugaFastFacts.map((fact) => (
              <div class="border-t border-on-surface-muted/20 py-4 md:grid md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-6">
                <dt class="text-label-sm text-on-surface uppercase tracking-widest md:col-span-4">{fact.label}</dt>
                <dd class="text-body-md text-on-surface-variant mt-2 md:mt-0 md:col-span-8">{fact.value}</dd>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ FAQ (Mississauga-specific, FAQPage schema) ═══ -->
  <section class="section-frame bg-surface-dim" style="padding: var(--spacing-section) 0;">
    <div class="container-editorial max-w-3xl">
      <div class="text-center mb-12 reveal">
        <h2 class="text-heading-lg font-serif italic">Questions I get about Mississauga</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal stagger-1">
        <FAQAccordion items={mississaugaFaq} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PortfolioFinalCTA
    title="Tell me about your Mississauga day."
    body="Send the date and the venue. I reply within 24 hours, and the first conversation is only about who is in the room and what the light will be doing when you get there."
    ctaLabel="Begin Your Journey"
    ctaHref="/contact/?location=mississauga#inquiry"
    background="background"
    image={heroImage}
    imageAlt="Natalie and Shavar hold hands beside her bouquet at their Glenerin Inn wedding in Mississauga, by AD Photography"
    imageCaption="Begin Your Journey"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .venue-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--spacing-block);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .venue-list {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      column-gap: var(--spacing-block);
    }
  }
  .venue-row__name {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--color-on-surface);
  }
  .venue-row__name:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }
  .venue-row__note {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .venue-row__links {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-on-surface-muted);
  }
  .venue-row__sep {
    margin: 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-on-surface-muted);
  }
  .underline-link {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    color: var(--color-on-surface);
    transition: color var(--duration-hover) var(--ease-gallery);
  }
  .underline-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }
</style>
